    "turn_text": "it's a hard job. It's a lot of travel. It's long hours. It's exhausting. You got to be on all the time. You got to be aware. You got to be paying attention. And the diversity of the work is extraordinary. And in many ways, it's very humbling. You recognize how much you have to learn, both in terms of parliamentary procedure, navigating Washington. And of course, the policy issue, areas that we dwell on every single day. So it has been humbling. It's been inspiring. And I, in many ways, I'm a freshman in Congress, and in some ways it's akin to feeling like a freshman in college. You're trying to find your way around. It is new. And you also start recognizing how much there is to learn, and I really relish that. And",
