  {
    "episode_id": 90843,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90843.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "House ethics. I had advocated to join the Foreign Affairs Committee because I think that we should be focused a lot more on diplomacy and our State Department. and using our national resources to pursue our national interests. And in my estimation, our foreign assistance budget right now is not used in the way that I think it can and should in ways that will build economic opportunity for people around the world and most of all enhance our safety and security in this country. So that is a focus of mine. And financial services was a committee that leadership asked me to join because of my experience in business and understanding the banking system and insurance and housing and whatnot. But it's a lot of meaty stuff. And no matter how much experience one brings to Congress, rest assured, they have a lot more to learn and I'm just one of them.",
