    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "we should at least consider and investigate because, yes, campaigning is constant and corresponding with campaigning is the relentless raising of money, the pursuit of money, which as you know is, because I talk about it all the time, is I think the most destructive and threatening issue that we have to deal with in this country. So I'd like to see shorter campaign windows, particularly as you recognize, a lot of people serving the public right now in the Senate and the House and other positions are now spending a lot of their time running around the country doing anything but the job that they're charged with doing. And that's not to say that you can't be a senator and run for president. In fact, I think it's a terrific stepping stone to doing so. But to do so for so many months, is something that I struggle",
