  {
    "episode_id": 90843,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90843.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "I'll say that when I first started running the notion of doing this every two years, it was something I struggled with, and I thought, boy, maybe we should look at you know, making a four-year terms or something. And then I'll tell you, when I've sworn into Congress and I've born witness to the inner workings and the dynamics that we face right now, I'm glad that we have two-year cycles because it is the mechanism by which the American public can register its either approval or disapproval in the middle of a four-year presidential term. I think our founders had designed the system remarkably well and attuned to possibilities and threats and it's frustrating sometimes but it's also I think a very important element of our Democratic Republic.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
