    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90843.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's analogous to the roof on a home. And nobody likes to come to the recognition that I've got to replace my roof. Nobody can see it. It's expensive. But if you don't do it, you can't even sleep at night because it's going to rain on you. Yes. And this is the same issue we have with infrastructure in this country. Some of it may not be the attractive, innovative projects that will redefine how a community looks, but it is the foundation through which we live our daily lives as individuals. It's the foundation of commerce in our country. It's the foundation of national security. The interstate highway system was initiated as a national defense strategy, and some people don't recall that. And by the way, it's not just roads and bridges. It's the electric",
